## Fixes applied (working tree, uncommitted)

**src/store.rs** — rewrote `elsewhere()` to search from the mirrored path (`worktree::main_root`) and accept the result only when `climb` did not leave the checkout (its existing `left_a_checkout` flag). This closes findings 1, 2, 5 and 12 in one change: the `Worktree` payload is now always a real main-checkout tracker, worktrees outside the main checkout are caught at any depth, the found ancestor is re-asked whether it redirects, and the eager climb plus the duplicate `main_root` walk are gone. Removed the `set_var` unit test (finding 3) — `tests/cli.rs::saying_where_init_goes_does_not_inherit_moai_here` already covers MOAI_HERE in a subprocess, which is the repo's documented technique. Added two regression tests; **both fail on the pre-fix body and pass after** (verified by reverting the body and re-running).

**src/read_marks.rs** — dropped `left.held.extend(then.held)` (8), moved `enum Wins` above the doc block so merge_past keeps its decision record (9), folded `stamped`/`outdated_by` onto one `stamp_of` accessor (11), and corrected two overclaiming doc passages (6, 7) plus the now-ambiguous review-8 inline comment.

**src/cmd/merge_driver.rs** — routed the sixth `canonicalize`-with-fallback copy through `store::real` and corrected `store::real`'s site list (10).

## Skipped

4 and 13 sit on explicit 2026-09-21 user decisions (spool merge policy; MOAI_HERE inheritance) — fixing either reopens the decision, so they are reported instead. 7 needs a new "what counts as a stamp" predicate shared by four readers. 14 needs a history rewrite. 15 is defensive code. Also noted and left alone: `scratch.rs`'s deliberate private `real` (the `#[path]` justification is technically correct), `hook::settled` vs `user_config::real_prefix`, and `overlay_later` vs `query::read_marks_of` — the last is blocked by the `query` purity rule.

